---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteChrome from '../components/SiteChrome.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { STATUS_LINE } from '../config/munchview';

/*
 * Who runs this studio, where it is, and what it has actually released.
 *
 * The homepage says what we build; this page says what exists. Those are
 * different claims and the site had only been making the first one — every
 * product was described in the present tense whether it had shipped or not,
 * and the only place the difference was written down was a comment in the
 * layout explaining why unreleased apps stay out of the structured data.
 *
 * The ledger below is that difference, made visible. Each row's status is the
 * SAME string the product's own page shows, so the two cannot drift apart:
 * change one and the other is already wrong in an obvious place. A status is
 * the first thing a partner, a tester or a store reviewer wants and the last
 * thing most studio sites will say plainly.
 */

/** Kept identical to the `status` line on each product page — see the note above. */
const ledger = [
  {
    name: 'SkyBattleSea',
    status: 'Live — free, in the browser',
    live: true,
    blurb: 'Fast planes against tanky ships. Five modes, eight craft classes, real multiplayer.',
    href: 'https://skybattlesea.com',
    external: true,
  },
  {
    name: 'Munchview',
    status: STATUS_LINE,
    live: false,
    blurb: 'Starts a good video that fits the time you have. Six platforms, one player, no feed.',
    href: '/munchview',
    external: false,
  },
  {
    name: 'EatStep',
    status: 'In development — Android APKs you can install today',
    live: false,
    blurb: 'Healthy food, ordered by the people who care what is in it. Three apps, one core.',
    href: '/eatstep',
    external: false,
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About — DeftDay Studio"
  description="DeftDay is an independent app and game studio in İzmir, Türkiye. What we have released, what is still being built, and what our apps deliberately do not do."
>
  <SiteChrome />

  <main class="page" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow">DeftDay Studio</p>
    <h1>A small studio in <span class="serif">İzmir.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We design, build and ship our own products — apps, games and small
      everyday utilities for iOS, Android and the web. No clients, no
      committees, nothing subcontracted. Everything on this site was made
      in-house.
    </p>

    <h2>What is live, and what is not</h2>
    <p>
      Studios have a habit of describing everything they are working on in the
      present tense. This is the real state of it. Each line says the same
      thing that product's own page says, and they change on the same day.
    </p>

    <ol class="ledger" role="list">
      {
        ledger.map((item) => (
          <li class="row rv">
            <div class="row-head">
              <h3 class="row-name">{item.name}</h3>
              <p class={item.live ? 'row-status is-live' : 'row-status'}>{item.status}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="row-blurb">{item.blurb}</p>
            <a
              class="row-link"
              href={item.href}
              {...(item.external ? { rel: 'noopener' } : {})}
              aria-label={`${item.name} — ${item.status}`}
            >
              {item.external ? 'Play it' : 'Read more'}
              {/* ↗ means "this leaves the site". Two of these three rows stay
                  on it, so they get the arrow that means "onward". */}
              <span aria-hidden="true">{item.external ? ' ↗' : ' →'}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <h2>How the work gets done</h2>
    <p>
      Product design, engineering, motion and store presence all happen here,
      which is the only reason a studio this size can hold one standard across
      several products at once. It also means there is nobody to hand a problem
      to: if something ships badly, it was us. The
      <a href="/#craft">craft section</a> on the homepage sets out what that covers.
    </p>
    <p>
      We would rather release one thing that behaves than three that
      demonstrate. That is why the list above is short and why two of its three
      rows still say they are not finished.
    </p>

    <h2>What our apps do not do</h2>
    <p>
      None of our apps carry trackers, and none of them build a profile of you
      to sell. Where an app stores something, it stores it on your own device
      unless you ask it to sync; where an account can be created, it can be
      deleted from inside the app and from the web without writing to anyone.
      The details, per app, are on the
      <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> — one section each, in plain language.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some of our apps will carry advertising and some never will.
      <strong>Munchview never will.</strong> It was promised without ads, it is
      paid for by its Pro upgrade, and that does not change later.
    </p>

    <h2>Where we are</h2>
    <p>
      DeftDay Studio, İzmir, Türkiye. Founded 2026. The fastest way to reach a
      person is <a href="mailto:hello@deftday.com">hello@deftday.com</a>; the
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a> says which address suits which kind of
      message.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    width: min(72ch, calc(100% - var(--gutter) * 2));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 140px 0 80px;
  }
  .page h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3rem);
    margin: 8px 0 16px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .page h2 {
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .page p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .page p + p {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .page strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .page a {
    color: var(--sun-text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .page a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /*
   * The ledger inverts the usual card: the STATUS is the coloured line, not
   * the product name. On a page whose whole point is "here is what actually
   * exists", the state is the information and the name is the label for it.
   */
  .ledger {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas:
      'head link'
      'blurb link';
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 4px 24px;
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .row-head {
    grid-area: head;
  }
  .row-name {
    font-family: var(--font-d);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  /*
   * Colour carries the state, so the page can be read without reading it:
   * warm means shipped, grey means not yet. Both statuses were warm at first
   * and the distinction the whole ledger exists to draw was invisible from
   * two feet away.
   */
  .row-status {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .row-status.is-live {
    background: var(--grad);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
  }
  .row-blurb {
    grid-area: blurb;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .row-link {
    grid-area: link;
    align-self: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .row-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-areas:
        'head'
        'blurb'
        'link';
      gap: 8px;
    }
    .row-link {
      align-self: start;
      margin-top: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
